    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for your interest in making Nvim better.\r\n\r\nBefore spending time reviewing this, let me set expectations:\r\n\r\n- Non-trivial PRs, especially new *features*, have a cost.\r\n    - If you don't plan to followup on problems for the foreseeable future, close the PR now.\r\n- Reviewing PRs takes a lot of time. Please plan to followup on review comments, or close this PR now.\r\n- Keep the PR rebased regularly, even if there's no feedback for weeks or months. This is the minimum gesture that increases our confidence that this isn't a drive-by contribution without an owner.\r\n- The project is extremely active, and that also means some PRs might sit around for quite awhile. You can greatly increase confidence in your work, and reduce reluctance to merge, by ensuring:\r\n    - PR description is in *concise* yet precise Problem/Solution format.\r\n    - Docs, code comments, names, etc., are concise and follow nearby conventions.\r\n    - You considered edge cases.\r\n    - Test coverage.\r\n    - Code was not duplicated.\r\n    - The \"interface\" considers existing precedent, and you reviewed `:help dev`.\r\n    - You read and applied [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md) and the [AI-assisted section](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#ai-assisted-work).\r\n- **Draft** PRs can ignore the above.\r\n    - If a non-Draft (\"Ready\") PR doesn't meet expectations, it will be closed without explanation.\r\n\r\nThe primary reason that PRs take longer to review/merge is because any of the above are lacking. Conversely, it's VERY EASY to click \"Merge\" when the work is thoughtful.",
