        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "at a glance this looks reasonable, the code is isolated to 2 functions in 1 module. but at least 2 things stand out:\r\n\r\n- the tests are somewhat verbose. some of the it() blocks might make sense as one it() block instead of over-granular cases\r\n- the code is non-trivial and has zero comments. over-commenting is bad, but giving 1-line hints/insights in key places is often very useful (often just an example says a lot more than a paragraph of prose)\r\n- the code grows an already-complex function. is there any opportunity for deduplication or factoring out some logic into local functions? keeping in mind that indirection also has a cost.",
